&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Company:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Faraday Future (FF) is a California-based embodied artificial intelligence ecosystem company, leveraging the latest technologies and world’s best talent to realize exciting new possibilities in mobility and robotics. We’re producing user-centric, technology-first vehicles and robots to establish new paradigms in human-AI interaction. We’re not just seeking to change how our cars and robots work – we’re seeking to change the way we drive and interact with machines. At FF, we’re creating something new, something connected, and something with a true global impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a senior marketing creative, centered on marketing creativity and a strong feel for localization, to join FF&#39;s brand marketing team. This mid-level role focuses on the U.S. market, with core responsibilities spanning two areas: first, leading the creative ideation and planning of product marketing content—turning AI, EV, and robotics product stories into bold, memorable content tuned to U.S. local context; and second, owning the social X (Twitter) presence and developing the founder&#39;s IP content, which represents the core strength of this role. The ideal candidate brings outstanding content creativity and localization instinct, deeply understands U.S. audiences and platform culture, and writes in a natural, well-paced, compelling voice—translating complex technology products into content and stories that resonate with U.S. consumers, rather than corporate-report or press-release style writing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead content ideation and planning for product marketing and promotion—starting from consumer insight and angle selection to shape memorable, locally-tuned creative concepts that make AI, EV, and robotics products more compelling in the U.S. market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day operation of the social X (Twitter) presence and the founder&#39;s IP content—planning posts and threads on AI, EV, robotics, and mobility topics, shaping an authentic, industry-savvy, conversation-driving voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write content across the full marketing funnel: social campaign copy, short-form video scripts, brand messaging, and product narratives for U.S. audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and design content for the website and e-commerce pages—shaping information architecture and visual storytelling to strengthen narrative, conversion, and brand consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay ahead of U.S. trends, cultural moments, and platform mechanics; localize content and plan social-native pieces built to travel and spark engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and write livestream talking points and host scripts to support product launches and promotional events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sales-conversion copy and scripts (landing pages, offers, CTAs, response scripts) that balance creativity with conversion goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, performance-marketing, and sales teams to align messaging from concept through publication and continuously optimize content performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI tools, platform analytics, and trend insights to accelerate ideation and improve content quality and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or above in Advertising, Marketing, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in content creative, marketing strategy, or brand/content creative; consumer or tech product experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Chinese/English bilingual ability, able to create fluent, natural English content with a good understanding of U.S. tone and cultural context, and solid content-localization ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at operating X (Twitter), with deep understanding of its content ecosystem, distribution mechanics, and account-growth playbook; experience running a brand or founder X account strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding content creativity and storytelling, able to independently run the full creative process from insight and angle to finished content—portfolio of content creative or marketing work required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid grounding in audiovisual language, able to produce scripts, storyboards, and cinematic narrative; sharp instinct for social and cultural moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with major U.S. social/content ecosystems (X, Instagram, YouTube, Reddit, TikTok); experience planning website, e-commerce, or landing-page content preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed and fast-moving, comfortable owning content end-to-end in a high-tempo environment.&lt;/li&gt;
