&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Company:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Faraday Future (FF) is a California-based mobility company, leveraging the latest technologies and world’s best talent to realize exciting new possibilities in mobility. We’re producing user-centric, technology-first vehicles to establish new paradigms in human-vehicle interaction. We’re not just seeking to change how our cars work – we’re seeking to change the way we drive. At FF, we’re creating something new, something connected, and something with a true global impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Your Role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job Description:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Robotics Data Operator&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Category:&amp;nbsp;Robotics / AI Data Operator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;LA, US&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a core member of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Robotics Data Factory&lt;/strong&gt;, you will be responsible for collecting high-fidelity human behavior and robot teleoperation data. This data is essential for training the next generation of Vision-Language-Action (VLA) models, helping robots learn to perceive and interact with the physical world by capturing real-world human interactions and precision robotic movements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Egocentric Data Collection:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Wear designated head-mounted recording devices (e.g., smartphone rigs, GoPro, or head-mounted VR kits) to capture daily or industrial tasks from a first-person perspective in diverse environments (home, retail, or manufacturing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VR Teleoperation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Operate robotic systems via VR interfaces to perform complex manipulation tasks. Ensure high-quality capture of multi-modal data, including joint states, torques, and gripper status, while maintaining low-latency execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Specification Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Maintain strict recording standards (1080p, 30FPS, horizontal orientation, FOV &amp;gt;130°). Ensure accurate extraction of camera intrinsic parameters and time-synchronization across all sensors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Assurance &amp;amp; Pre-processing:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Conduct initial self-inspections to filter out clips with excessive shaking, occlusions, or focus failures. Ensure data is correctly formatted (e.g., MCAP, HDF5) and uploaded according to protocol.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Basic Qualifications:&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;0–1 years of experience. Currently pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Computer Science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extreme Attention to Detail:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Ability to strictly follow complex technical guidelines regarding framing, motion rhythm, and lighting environments.&lt;/li&gt;
